<section id="days">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">How the five days run</p>
        <h2>Interviews, your own data, and a readout in person.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="sub">The clock starts once we have usable exports. We keep the ask on your team small, and most of the work happens on our side.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step"><div class="n">DAY 1</div><h3>MAP</h3><p>Interviews with management and department leads, and a walk through the store. We learn how work actually moves, not how the org chart says it does.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="n">DAY 2</div><h3>VERIFY</h3><p>We check whether your CRM and DMS exports can actually answer the question, remove customer-identifying details, then measure where work waits. If the data can't support a finding, we tell you.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="n">DAY 3</div><h3>FIND</h3><p>Where work waits, loses its owner, gets duplicated or drops out of view, and whether a tool you already pay for could fix it.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="n">DAY 4</div><h3>PRIORITIZE</h3><p>Opportunities ranked on impact, strength of evidence, effort, risk and whether your people will actually use it.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="n">DAY 5</div><h3>READOUT</h3><p>We walk leadership through the findings in person and recommend a first project. You keep the full report.</p></div>
      <div class="step last"><div class="n">AFTER</div><h3>YOUR CALL</h3><p>Implementation is scoped from what we found, with a baseline set before anything is built. There's no obligation to continue.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

